    "notes": [
      "AdditionalTools.id is an optional nullable ResponseItemId with serde default and skip-none: None is omitted from the wire and a Some(id) value is preserved, so a 0.149 client can carry a set identifier.",
      "ResponseItemId is a serde-transparent string without an upstream byte bound. The first captured/constructed 0.149 declaration uses None, but the upstream 0.149 models.rs test sets an at_ prefixed identifier (at_test), so absence in one capture is not a wire-level prohibition.",
      "The 128-byte cap, ASCII character set, and secret-shape rejections are the gateway's own bounded subset consistent with its existing Codex item-ID convention; they do not describe upstream behavior.",
      "The gateway does not treat the identifier as identity, replay, or audit authority."
    ],
